# Matching Parts of a Value

- `[attr^="val"]` – value starts with `val`.
- `[attr$="val"]` – value ends with `val`.
- `[attr*="val"]` – value contains `val` anywhere.
- `[attr~="val"]` – value contains `val` as a whole word (space‑separated).
- `[attr|="val"]` – value is exactly `val` or starts with `val-` (for language codes).

```css
/* all external links (href starts with http) */
a[href^="http"] { color: purple; }
/* all PDF links (href ends with .pdf) */
a[href$=".pdf"] { font-weight: bold; }
```

slides.codeSnippet:
input[type="email"] {
  border-color: dodgerblue;
}
input[type="submit"] {
  background: #27ae60;
  color: white;
  border: none;
}
a[href*="example"] {
  text-decoration: underline wavy;
}

slides.content:
# Add `i` Before the Closing Bracket

```css
/* matches type="TEXT", type="text", type="Text" */
input[type="text" i] {
  background: #f9f9f9;
}
```
The `i` flag tells the browser to ignore case. Works for all attribute selectors except `~=` (which already uses its own rules).
